  "facts": [
    "Måløy Bridge, Norway's longest at its 1974 opening, stretched 1,224 metres across the strait, featuring 34 spans and a 125‑metre main span that still impresses engineers today.",
    "Construction began in 1971, and the bridge opened to traffic in December 1973, but the ceremonial ribbon‑cutting by King Olav V was delayed by a storm‑hit Royal Yacht, arriving a day late.",
    "Designed to withstand winds up to 75 metres per second, the bridge still closes for high gusts, with side boards displaying real‑time wind speeds that can reach 170 miles per hour."
